<%#
  Action Settings footer (issue #1024)

  Closes an action Property Inspector's OWN settings with the way through to
  everything that is not on this page: the iRaceDeck Settings window.

  It sits here, and not at the bottom where #1003 first put it, because since
  #1003 the window owns every plugin-wide setting — which makes this the
  most-used control on a Property Inspector, and it had ended up as the last
  thing on the page, a scroll past four override accordions and the Key
  Bindings section away. Under the action's own settings is as high as it can
  go: the panel's first row is the deck software's own Title field, and nothing
  can render above that.

  It also lands on an honest boundary. Everything BELOW it — title, colour,
  border and graphic overrides, flags — is this one key's appearance; everything
  BEHIND it is every key's.

  PLACEMENT RULE, the one thing to get right: include this AFTER the action's
  own settings and BEFORE the key-icon appearance block, OUTSIDE every
  surface-conditional wrapper. On the 16 dial-capable PIs the appearance block
  lives inside `<div id="keypad-appearance">`, which the PI hides on the dial
  surface (a dial has no key icon) — anchored in there, the button would vanish
  for every dial user, whose settings-window trip is exactly as long as anyone
  else's. `action-settings-footer-partial.test.ts` checks the placement in all
  35 templates so this comment is not the only thing holding it.

  `ird-section-footer` draws the divider above the button, the same rule the
  docs link uses to close the page. The button itself, its warning banner and
  the reason they travel together live in `open-settings.ejs`.
%>
<%- include('open-settings', { extraClass: 'ird-section-footer' }) %>
